  data: {
    LLM: 'Play proceeds in tricks. A lead may be a legal ordinary combination or bomb. Each following play must be the same combination type and exactly one rank higher, or a permitted special response such as a two-set on singles/pairs, or a bomb. Players may pass. When all but one player pass, the trick ends; players draw from the talon starting with the last player to play, then that player leads the next trick.',
    Player: 'Play proceeds in tricks. A lead may be a legal ordinary combination or bomb. Each following play must be the same combination type and exactly one rank higher, or a permitted special response such as a two-set on singles/pairs, or a bomb. Players may pass. When all but one player pass, the trick ends; players draw from the talon starting with the last player to play, then that player leads the next trick.',
    objective: 'Be the first player to shed all cards from hand; if you cannot win, minimize cards left when another player goes out.',
    gameplay: 'Play proceeds in tricks. A lead may be a legal ordinary combination or bomb. Each following play must be the same combination type and exactly one rank higher, or a permitted special response such as a two-set on singles/pairs, or a bomb. Players may pass. When all but one player pass, the trick ends; players draw from the talon starting with the last player to play, then that player leads the next trick.',
    keyRules: [
      'Singles, pairs, sequences, and double-sequences are ordinary combinations; responses must usually be exactly one rank higher.',
      'Twos are highest in singles and pairs but cannot be used inside sequences or double-sequences.',
      'Bombs (triples, four-of-a-kind, and double-joker bomb) can beat ordinary combinations, with larger bomb classes beating smaller ones.',
      'Jokers are wild in combinations but cannot normally be played as single cards unless it is your only remaining card when leading.',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: false,
    trumpBonusValues: null,
    setup: {
      players: '2 to 6 players, with each player competing individually.',
      deck: '54-card deck (standard 52 cards plus two jokers).',
      equipment: 'Standard deck + 2 jokers',
      dealing: 'Dealer shuffles, then players draw cards in counterclockwise order until dealer has 6 cards and each other player has 5. Remaining cards form a face-down talon.',
    },
    turnFlow: 'Play proceeds in tricks. A lead may be a legal ordinary combination or bomb. Each following play must be the same combination type and exactly one rank higher, or a permitted special response such as a two-set on singles/pairs, or a bomb. Players may pass. When all but one player pass, the trick ends; players draw from the talon starting with the last player to play, then that player leads the next trick.',
    moveValidityConditions: {
      ante: 'Gan Deng Yan has no ante mechanic; hands start from a fixed deal.',
      deal: 'Dealer only at the beginning of each deal.',
      reveal_market: 'No market row exists in this climbing game.',
      buy_market: 'Cards are not bought from any market in Gan Deng Yan.',
      buy_stock: 'Players draw from the talon by rule; there is no stock purchase.',
      fold: 'Players may pass a turn but cannot fold out of an active deal.',
      check: 'There is no betting round where a check action applies.',
      call: 'Gan Deng Yan has no wager matching or call mechanic.',
      bet: 'No betting structure is used in standard Gan Deng Yan play.',
      raise: 'No betting structure exists, so raising is not applicable.',
      declare: 'This game ends by shedding cards, not by declaration actions.',
      reveal_hand: 'Hands stay private; there is no reveal-hand step in core rules.',
      award_pot: 'System action at end of deal after a player goes out.',
      play_card: 'Must be same type and exactly one rank higher than prior ordinary play, unless using a permitted special response or bomb.',
      draw: 'Only during trick-end refill and only while talon has cards remaining.',
      discard: 'Cards are played to tricks, not discarded by separate discard action.',
      pass: 'Allowed on your turn during a trick; once everyone else passes, trick ends.',
      bid: 'No bidding phase exists in Gan Deng Yan.',
      meld: 'The game uses climbing combinations, not persistent meld-laying.',
      go_out: 'Triggers immediately when a legal play empties your hand.',
    },
    exampleHands: [
      'Setup example: 6 card(s) per player.',
      'Rule example: Be the first player to shed all cards from hand; if you cannot win, minimize cards left when another player goes out.',
      'Turn-flow example: Play proceeds in tricks. A lead may be a legal ordinary combination or bomb. Each following play must be the same combination type and exactly one rank higher, or a permitted special response such as a two-set on singles/pairs, or a bomb. Players may pass. When all but one player pass, the trick ends; players draw from the talon starting with the last player to play, then that player leads the next trick.',
      'Scoring example: Winner scores one point from each opponent for every card that opponent still holds at the end of the deal. First to shed all cards..',
